    window.ASSESS_NARR = {
head_gut:['You\u2019re an analytical thinker. You reach for data, evidence, and structured reasoning. Your strength is thoroughness; your risk is analysis paralysis and dismissing valid intuitions.','You blend analysis and intuition. You gather data but also listen to gut signals. The challenge is knowing which mode to trust in a given situation.','You\u2019re an intuitive decider. You read situations quickly and trust the signal your experience generates. Your strength is speed and pattern recognition; your risk is post-hoc rationalization \u2014 building the case after you\u2019ve already decided.'],
fast_slow:['You decide quickly. Once you see it, you\u2019re ready to move. Your strength is momentum; your risk is that speed can feel like certainty when it\u2019s actually impatience.','Your tempo depends on the stakes. You can move fast when needed and slow down when it matters. The question is whether you\u2019re genuinely matching speed to situation, or defaulting to whatever feels most comfortable.','You\u2019re a deliberate decider. You need time to sit with things, turn them over, let the picture develop. Your strength is considered judgment; your risk is that \u201Cthinking more\u201D becomes a way to avoid committing.'],
bold_cautious:['You lean bold. Uncertainty energizes rather than paralyzes you. You\u2019re comfortable with incomplete information and willing to bet. Your risk is underweighting genuine downside.','You balance risk and caution depending on context. You neither chase nor avoid uncertainty. The question is whether you\u2019re calibrating well, or just averaging out competing impulses.','You\u2019re cautious by nature. You want the downside understood and contained before you commit. Your strength is protecting against catastrophic outcomes; your risk is that excessive caution becomes inaction.'],
solo_social:['You decide independently. You process internally and announce. Your strength is clarity \u2014 you don\u2019t get swayed by committees. Your risk is blind spots that other perspectives would have caught.','You consult selectively. You\u2019re open to input but don\u2019t need consensus. The question is whether you\u2019re choosing the right people to listen to, or just the comfortable ones.','You\u2019re a consultative decider. You think out loud and draw on others\u2019 perspectives. Your strength is diverse input; your risk is decision-by-committee or outsourcing your judgment.'],
opt_prag:['You\u2019re an optimizer. You keep searching, comparing, and refining. You want the best option, not just a good one. Your strength is thoroughness; your risk is that the search never ends.','You calibrate your search to the stakes. Big decisions get more exploration; small ones get resolved quickly. This is healthy \u2014 as long as it\u2019s intentional rather than habitual.','You\u2019re a pragmatist. When something meets the bar, you commit and move on. Your strength is decisiveness and efficiency; your risk is leaving better options undiscovered.']};
